From dd13b881139d5e925686a4c134c21f7a73cae357 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:20:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: the Logging table says what each column holds, and
 Addons opens

Firewall > Logging had its first two heads transposed - Time over the action
badge, Action over the timestamp - and a third reading "Chain" over a column
showing the inbound interface. The row now reads Action, Time, Interface and
on, matching the cells one for one, using the stock <#wan_interface#> token.

The viewer's classOf() matched only "REAPER-WARDEN", so the -OUT and -SELF
prefixes collapsed back into a single WARDEN badge, undoing the separation
they exist for. All three are told apart again.

Addons was the one rail item that did not navigate: it unfolded a sub-list.
It is now an ordinary item that opens the first addon page, with its siblings
arriving as the shell's tab bar, changed in both rails in lockstep.

The dashboard firmware pill gains a BETA chip read off EXTENDNO, and the
About page stops treating a channel suffix as a version mismatch - the patch
series is stamped bare, so "v3.1.2_BETA" would otherwise have fired the
"series as of vX" qualifier on every beta build, which is the one thing that
line exists not to do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
